  "question": {
    "text": "The synthesis of alkyl fluorides is best accomplished by:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Swarts reaction",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Free radical fluorination",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Sandmeyer's  reaction",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Finkelstein reaction",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Alkyl fluorides is best accomplished by swarts reaction i.e. heating an alkyl chloride/bromide in the presence of metallic fluoride such as AgF, Hg<sub>2</sub>F<sub>2</sub>, CoF<sub>2</sub>, SbF<sub>3</sub>.<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>CH</mtext> <mn>3</mn> </msub> <mtext>Br</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>AgF</mtext> <mo>→</mo> <msub> <mtext>CH</mtext> <mn>3</mn></msub><mtext>F</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>AgBr</mtext> </mrow> </math>"
  }
}